{
  "dimension": "Non-Judgmental Language",
  "polarity": "positive",
  "cluster_id": 11,
  "patient": "The other day, I overheard Jenny saying something to her dad about feeling like the abuse was her fault. And obviously as a parent, that's really difficult to hear. But then I just kept worrying about it and thinking about it and I talked to my friends and I talked to my mom and they all just told me that neither of us were thinking about this in a helpful way, but what happened to her was so terrible I don't know how else to think about it.",
  "therapist": "Yeah. So what you're describing is actually pretty common for parents and kids who've gone through what you guys have gone through. And it's actually one of the things that we'll talk about in therapy. And we'll kind of help you identify what thoughts you're having about it that might be more inaccurate or unhelpful and kind of help you reframe it so that you can think about it in a different way to alleviate some of that distress.",
